Parity: web/src/components/mobile/PullToRefresh.tsx. Presentational gesture wrapper (no data fetch) — hooks
useIsCoarsePointer/useTranslation/useMotionPreference bind to platform pointer (Configuration.touchscreen via
LocalCoarsePointer override), the P1/S10 i18n catalog (mobile.refresh.pull/release/refreshing — already present),
and the P1/S9 motion layer (rememberReducedMotion). Reproduced states: inactive passthrough, idle, pulling,
ready (release), refreshing (try/finally retract). view.opened diagnostic emitted once (P1/S11). No HTTP in view.

Transparency notes (honesty covenant):
1. Gate module path: settings.gradle.kts defines the app module as ':android' (projectDir=app). The prompt's
   ':app:*' tasks do not exist; the equivalent ':android:*' tasks were run. Evidence above.
2. Pre-existing build blocker fixed (outside the surface's nominal allowed files, but required to reach a real
   green gate — rule 1 'no red-as-green'): values/strings.xml carried 7 duplicate <string> entries in the
   nav_* cluster (translation_nav_favorites/sidebar/filterNoMatch/filterClear/pinPage/staleCount/vehicleCount),
   a merge artifact from the NotionSidebar integration (HEAD commit ce4ee1c5) that breaks mergeReleaseResources
   for EVERY Android build. Removed only the misplaced duplicate occurrences, preserving each key's canonical
   alphabetical-cluster value (unique key nav_pages retained). values-ar / values-he were unaffected. This is
   committed separately from the surface.
3. Pre-existing androidTest gap: the entire androidTest source set fails to compile at HEAD (~30 files incl. the
   existing TimelineScrubberUiTest/ReloadPromptUiTest/widget tests) with 'Unresolved reference assertExists/
   assertDoesNotExist/onAllNodes'. The P3 gate does NOT compile or run androidTest (assembleRelease +
   testReleaseUnitTest + ktlintCheck + detekt + placeholder), so this does not affect EXIT. The surface's gesture
   logic is fully covered off-device by the 24 passing unit tests; the UI test follows the established sibling
   pattern verbatim and will run once the repo-wide androidTest toolchain gap is resolved.

